  "narrative": "The due validation of the feature_006 screen for outcome_014 closes that route as unsupported by clinically meaningful evidence. H163 was a registered main-effect contrast for feature_006=1 versus feature_006=0 on outcome_014. Its discovery evidence, R149, showed a large signed negative contrast of about -0.0647 with interval -0.1186 to -0.0108. Relative to the approximate outcome_014 clinical threshold based on a 10% difference in the absolute mean dependency magnitude, around 0.0093, this discovery point and interval were threshold-compatible in the direction opposite to the registered claim, indicating that feature_006=1 appeared to have a more negative outcome_014 score, i.e. stronger apparent dependency, in the discovery cells. However, independent validation, R150, reversed the direction and was imprecise: signed estimate about +0.0360 with adjusted interval -0.0522 to +0.1242. The validation interval spans zero and does not provide multiplicity-adjusted support for either the registered positive direction or the reverse negative direction. Because the validation was direction-discordant and not threshold-discriminating, I reject H163 and close it. For the same reason I reject and close the reverse claim H164: its validation evidence is also the mirror-image nonconfirmation of the reverse hypothesis. I close H165-H167 as unresolved rather than active or rejected; they are untested coherence endpoints for feature_006, and after the parent main contrast failed replication, they would likely chase a false lead rather than provide scientific information. No new validation request is made because no remaining request is available and, more importantly, no claim is currently worth validating. The broader synthesis remains that no clinically meaningful predictor-subgroup association has been established in this dataset. The strongest scientifically informative conclusion is not a positive dependency-marker association, but a reproducible pattern of nonconfirmation. Validated or coherence-failed routes include feature_047 with outcome_013, the feature_045 subgroup routes for outcome_014 and outcome_006, the feature_023 interaction family for outcome_014, the feature_027 outcome_013 signal, several feature_060 and feature_034 subgroup or outcome-specific routes, the feature_060 within feature_002 outcome_014/008/013/011 panel, the feature_001 main-effect panel, and the feature_036 level_002 versus level_001 panel. These negative findings should be understood as failure to support a clinically meaningful 10%-scale association under the current comparisons and uncertainty; many intervals are wide enough that small or subthreshold associations cannot be excluded. The current unresolved items are not accepted findings. H136 remains scientifically curious because its independent validation suggested a large reverse outcome_014 contrast in the feature_002=0 subgroup, but its discovery evidence was directionally opposite and its coherence panel failed, especially through H138. H26, H12, H37, and H42 remain near-threshold subgroup signals for feature_060 and outcome_001, but they lack direction-coherent and threshold-discriminating evidence. H7 and H10 remain imprecise main-effect leads. Many other predictors have not received adequate broad screening. Therefore the most informative next analysis is to activate the deferred untested screen covering feature_063 on outcome_014, outcome_013, outcome_012, and outcome_011; feature_055 level_003 versus level_001 on outcome_011 and outcome_016; feature_042 on outcome_014, outcome_001, and outcome_008; feature_007 on outcome_014 and outcome_013; and feature_005 on outcome_014. This batch preserves breadth, uses predictors with adequate cell counts, avoids refocusing on routes that failed validation or coherence, and allows a new candidate to be identified only if it is direction-consistent across related outcomes, threshold-compatible under the outcome-specific 10% scale, and not explained by sparse cells or precision alone. All statements remain within-dataset associations and do not imply causality or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Round 12 synthesis: No accepted claims. H163 feature_006 outcome_014 was rejected after independent validation reversed direction and was imprecise; R149 discovery showed large opposite contrast, but R150 validation was signed positive about 0.036 with adjusted interval -0.052 to 0.124. H164 reverse route rejected for the same reason. H165-H167 coherence endpoints closed unresolved because the parent feature_006 main contrast failed replication and they are untested. No further validation is requested. Overall scientific conclusion: no measured predictor or subgroup has an accepted clinically meaningful association with the 16 dependency outcomes under the 10% relative outcome-magnitude standard. The evidence landscape is dominated by negative or nonreplicated findings: feature_047 outcome_013, feature_045 subgroup routes outcome_014 and outcome_006, feature_023 outcome_014 interaction family, feature_027 outcome_013, feature_060 outcome_001 and outcome_006 subgroup routes, feature_034 outcome_006/001 routes, feature_060-within-feature_002 outcome_014/008/013/011 panel, feature_001 main-effect panel, and feature_036 level_002 versus level_001 panel all fail coherence or threshold-discriminating precision. These are negative evidence for the registered hypotheses, not proof of absence, especially for wide intervals. Remaining unresolved leads include H136 discordant feature_045 feature_002=0 outcome_014 subgroup, near-threshold feature_060 outcome_001 subgroup signals H26 H12 H37 H42, feature_001 H7, feature_065 H10, and untested features. Next active plan: execute 12 deferred untested broad screens. H131-H133: feature_042 on outcome_014 outcome_001 outcome_008. H134-H135: feature_007 on outcome_014 outcome_013. H145-H148: feature_063 level_001 versus level_002 on outcome_014 outcome_013 outcome_012 outcome_011. H149-H150: feature_055 level_003 versus level_001 on outcome_011 outcome_016. H151: feature_005 on outcome_014. Evaluate any new signal using outcome-specific 10% absolute mean magnitude thresholds: approximate values include outcome_014 0.0093, outcome_006 0.0175, outcome_013 0.0269, outcome_012 0.0248, outcome_011 0.0301, outcome_016 0.0256, outcome_008 0.0282, outcome_001 0.0415. Accept only if direction is coherent across related outcomes and intervals are threshold-discriminating; otherwise reject or close. Avoid returning to failed feature_045/030/047/023/027/060/034 routes unless a new independent coherent discovery arises. All claims remain within-dataset associations."
